  "about": {
    "caption": "Who's driving?",
    "lead": "I'm Sriram. I build things people can play with, and tools that are honest about how they work.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "So far that has meant a live cricket auction game, a 3D multiplayer prop hunt, a tool that tracks how a codebase's architecture drifts over time, and a video clipper that runs entirely on my own laptop.",
      "I'm in my fourth year of a B.Tech in Computer Science and Engineering, specialising in AI and machine learning, at VIT Chennai. I graduate in 2027.",
      "I'm from Berhampur and study in Chennai. Outside code I'm into cricket, gaming, video editing and creative design, and I like taking random ideas and seeing whether I can turn them into something that actually works.",
      "Next, I want to work on hard problems in AI and machine learning, agentic systems, back ends and distributed systems, and build products where AI is genuinely useful, not added for the sake of it. I also want to get better at system design and at building things that are ready for production."
    ]
